  "result": "Completion now handles arguments containing `#`. The change is in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped, so `prog a#b c` was parsed as `prog a`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is a normal character. A quick check now gives `['prog', 'a#b', 'c']` and `['prog', '#x']`. The 58 tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass; I didn't run the rest of the suite.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for `#`. I can add one if you want.",
